both call, or add a test that feeds the same synthetic per-ticket event dict to both implementations and asserts equality.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the per-ticket failure policy for the show_ticket/event-read loop (record and skip the failing ticket vs. abort), and surface skipped tickets in the report rather than swallowing them.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"per store_name, tracker_git_root in store_roots ... around show_ticket(ticket_id, include_inbound=True)\"","AC[1]: \"each ticket needs its own show_ticket call, too slow at that scale\" — confirms a large per-ticket fan-out.","Absence: no statement of what happens when one show_ticket / _batch_cat read raises (skip-and-record vs. abort)."],"finding":"The plan performs one show_ticket call per ticket across a large corpus (AC[1] cites ~6400 tickets) but never specifies error handling when an individual show_ticket / event read fails. Without a stated per-ticket failure policy, a single raising ticket aborts the whole labels build with no partial output, and the failure of one store's tracker access is not surfaced as a degraded result.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f94b75bda69754c71","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Ticket-level event source' and 'Ticket-level labels'","norm_id":"n485817fb430b4427","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A single malformed/missing ticket event during a multi-thousand-ticket run raises → entire labels build fails with no labels-<hash>.jsonl written, wasting the whole pass.","A tracker_git_root that is temporarily unavailable takes down labeling for every store, not just its own."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Wrap the per-ticket event fetch so a failure records the ticket_id + error into the report's diagnostics and continues, keeping already-derived labels durable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge the criteria-load-shift confound in norm_id-keyed per-criterion churn, and state why norm_id (criteria-baked) is preferred over fix_unit_key (criteria-free) for the churn sets — or switch the churn join to fix_unit_key.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a finding's norm_id is a member of EVERY criterion in its criteria list; churn(c) = 1 - jaccard(S_k(c), S_{k+1}(c))'","sidecar.norm_id: basis = tokens + '|' + ','.join(sorted(finding['criteria'])) — the criteria set is part of the hash","sidecar.fix_unit_key docstring: 'norm_id cannot serve here — it bakes the sorted criteria list into its hash, so one defect co-cited by N criteria mints N distinct norm_ids'","This confounds churn (criteria-load change) with resolution across a differing-material pair, which is what churn purports to measure"],"finding":"The per-criterion churn mechanism keys criterion membership sets on sidecar.norm_id, but norm_id bakes the finding's SORTED CRITERIA SET into its hash. So a defect co-cited by ['E2','T8'] mints ONE norm_id keyed to 'E2,T8'; if a differing-material re-review re-raises the same defect under a shifted criteria load (e.g. only ['E2']), the norm_id changes, and the persisted defect reads as FULL churn on both E2 and T8 — a criteria-load-shift confound that inflates the published floor. The codebase documents fix_unit_key (criteria-free) as the correct join basis for exactly this reason.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f46a5ebae299884c6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § 'Noise floor' (b) per-criterion churn","norm_id":"nb70aea9ce11dba6c","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A finding re-raised on the next review with a narrowed or widened criteria list (common as reviewers refine attribution) counts as full churn on every criterion despite the defect persisting"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concurrency/ownership assumption for the REBAR_TRACKER_DIR global mutation (single-threaded ownership, or pass tracker_git_root explicitly to show_ticket instead of mutating a process-global).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"temporarily set os.environ[\\\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\\\"] = tracker_git_root (restored finally) around show_ticket(...)\"","Context: \"config.tracker_dir_override() reads REBAR_TRACKER_DIR, winning verbatim over any config.\"","No statement that build_labels owns the process exclusively or runs single-threaded during the mutation window."],"finding":"The plan mutates the process-global env var os.environ['REBAR_TRACKER_DIR'] inside a per-store loop and relies on show_ticket/config.tracker_dir_override consuming it, restoring only in finally. The finally handles the retire/restore lifecycle but the plan states no ownership or concurrency guarantee for this global: if build_labels ever runs alongside any other in-process rebar code (or is parallelized over stores), one store's override leaks into another consumer's tracker resolution, since the env var is read verbatim and 'winning over any config'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5e2bd8648147571e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Ticket-level event source (multi-store, env override)'","norm_id":"n755632665f93a582","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["build_labels invoked in a process where any other rebar operation reads REBAR_TRACKER_DIR concurrently → that operation resolves the wrong tracker for the duration of a show_ticket call.","A future parallelization over store_roots races on the single global env var → cross-store ticket resolution."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Prefer passing the tracker root to show_ticket via an explicit argument/context rather than mutating os.environ; if the env mutation must stand, document that build_labels requires exclusive single-threaded ownership of the process during the loop.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State why the per-ticket show_ticket call is preferred over deriving close_class from the existing bulk event walk plus a single caused_by target-index, OR adopt the bulk approach so the full-corpus run is not blocked on O(N) show_ticket cost.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'per store_name, tracker_git_root in store_roots, temporarily set os.environ[\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\"]... around show_ticket(ticket_id, include_inbound=True)'","AC1: 'A full-corpus (~6400-ticket) run is DEFERRED follow-up: each ticket needs its own show_ticket call, too slow at that scale... confirmed per-call cost, not lock contention'","close_class is persisted on the close STATUS event (tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py reads close_class off the close event data; tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py confirms the close transition folds close_class into state) — so it needs no show_ticket call","The plan already reimplements reopen_count/force_close/completion_verifier_fail_count over the bulk _enumerate_event_blobs walk, so extending the walk to also emit close_class is a small, already-chosen pattern"],"finding":"The ticket-level event source uses a per-ticket show_ticket call for escaped_defect (close_class + caused_by), which AC1 identifies as the reason the full ~6400-ticket corpus run is deferred as 'too slow'; a single bulk-walk alternative was likely missed. close_class is persisted on the close STATUS event, so it is derivable from the SAME corpus._enumerate_event_blobs + _batch_cat walk the plan already performs for reopen_count/force_close/completion_verifier_fail_count. Only the INBOUND caused_by edge needs cross-ticket resolution, which can be satisfied by building one caused_by target-index over all bug tickets' OUTBOUND caused_by links in a single walk rather than N show_ticket calls.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59575139cdf02316","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § 'Ticket-level event source (multi-store, env override)' + Acceptance Criteria AC1","norm_id":"n6f80036e5010d468","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running build_labels over the full store where the O(N) show_ticket cost is prohibitive — the plan's stated deferred scope","A caused_by edge index built once lets escaped_defect resolve the inbound relation without a per-ticket lookup"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Derive close_class from the close STATUS event in the same _enumerate_event_blobs+_batch_cat walk (as reopen/force_close already are), and build a one-pass caused_by target-index over all bugs' outbound caused_by links; reserve show_ticket only if a field genuinely cannot be recovered from the event stream.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"6fc00cb8dbd412e6","material_parts":{"children":["